  "id": "COMPOUND:18725 - PROTEIN:5011",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but interconnected pathway linking the compound 2-[[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]-2H-furan-5-one to HCC1937 through multiple targets. The compound is directly linked to 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is a known target of several compounds, including 5-Oxobrucine and Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside. These targets are all implicated in cellular processes that may influence the progression of HCC1937, a cancer cell line. The evidence suggests that the compound may exert its effects through the modulation of proteasome activity, which is a critical pathway in cell survival and tumor progression. The integration of these targets implies that the compound may act as a modulator of proteasome function, potentially influencing HCC1937 through a mechanism involving the regulation of cellular processes that are central to cancer development.",
